/>\n\tHit Ratio = Page Hits / Total Accesses = 3 / 12 = 0.25 or 25% (10%)</strong><br />\n\t&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t<p data-end=\"445\" data-start=\"248\"><strong data-end=\"268\" data-start=\"248\">Belady&rsquo;s Anomaly</strong> refers to the counterintuitive situation in <strong data-end=\"348\" data-start=\"313\">FIFO Page Replacement Algorithm</strong> where <strong data-end=\"395\" data-start=\"355\">increasing the number of page frames</strong> results in <strong data-end=\"427\" data-start=\"407\">more page faults</strong> instead of fewer.</p>\n\n\t<p data-end=\"528\" data-start=\"447\">This anomaly occurs <strong data-end=\"485\" data-start=\"469\">only in FIFO</strong>, not in <strong data-end=\"501\" data-start=\"494\">LRU</strong> or <strong data-end=\"516\" data-start=\"505\">Optimal</strong> algorithms.<br />\n\t<br />\n\t&nbsp;</p>\n\n\t<h3 data-end=\"1420\" data-start=\"1388\"><strong data-end=\"1420\" data-start=\"1395\">Case 2: 4 Page Frames&nbsp; (30%)</strong></h3>\n\n\t<table data-end=\"2103\" data-start=\"1422\">\n\t\t<thead data-end=\"1469\" data-start=\"1422\">\n\t\t\t<tr data-end=\"1469\" data-start=\"1422\">\n\t\t\t\t<th data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1429\" data-start=\"1422\">Step</th>\n\t\t\t\t<th data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1436\" data-start=\"1429\">Page</th>\n\t\t\t\t<th data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1455\" data-start=\"1436\">Frames</th>\n\t\t\t\t<th data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1469\" data-start=\"1455\">Page Fault</th>\n\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t</thead>\n\t\t<tbody data-end=\"2103\" data-start=\"1518\">\n\t\t\t<tr data-end=\"1566\" data-start=\"1518\">\n\t\t\t\t<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1525\" data-start=\"1518\">1</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1532\" data-start=\"1525\">1</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1551\" data-start=\"1532\">1 _ _ _</td>\n\t\t\t\t<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-end=\"1566\" data-start=\"1551\">\u2714\ufe0f</td>\n\t\t\t</tr>\n\t\t\t<tr data-end=\"1615\" data-start=\"156