ata-end=\"2483\" data-start=\"2456\">&nbsp;Why does this happen? (10%)</h2>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2555\" data-start=\"2485\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2555\" data-start=\"2487\">FIFO doesn&#39;t consider how <em data-end=\"2523\" data-start=\"2513\">recently</em> or <em data-end=\"2539\" data-start=\"2527\">frequently</em> a page is used.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2671\" data-start=\"2556\">\n\t<p data-end=\"2671\" data-start=\"2558\">So, adding more frames can sometimes lead to <strong data-end=\"2641\" data-start=\"2603\">earlier useful pages being removed</strong> earlier, causing more faults.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
